                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_601">Worcester,
                            Worcestershire, Benedictine cathedral priory of St Mary the
                            Virgin</orgName> <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition
                            of Medieval Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in
                            the Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                            Britain index card was originally written for Cambridge, Trinity
                            College, MS B. 4. 24, but then extended to also cover Cambridge, Corpus
                            Christi College, MS 87. The card records the following reason for a
                            potential attribution: '"Perhaps from Worcester" (M. R. James), owing to
                            the old velvet binding, found also on Cambridge, Corpus Christi College,
                            MSS 87 and 217.' However, Ker later added a query on the card: 'Isn't
                            this a Henry VIII binding.'</p></provenance>
                    </history>
